 "note": "RPCS3 Core 917 = Core 916 plus the first work on the cost of the exact reservation write lock, for Call of Duty: Black Ops II (build 676, the last export that holds its report windows: 1.08 to 1.60 million heavy PUTLLC locks per 5 s window, 1.8 to 2.5 us to acquire each, 12 ns to hold it, 20 to 26 frames per second with no thread saturated). REWINDBOX_WRITER_PARK_SPIN_917: a writer that waits for the PPU threads to park spins for 8 us in a loop in front of its previous wait, which is untouched; its own setting, Automatic = every title, Disabled = the previous wait. REWINDBOX_PARK_SPIN_COMPARE_917: on Automatic, in a storm of heavy PUTLLC the report turns the lever off and on again between its windows (after 6 storm windows of a boot, 2 off and 2 on in turn for 16 windows, then on) so that one export holds both sides in the same scene. RANGELOCKPROF reports the park phase by duration, the slow-park time, the locks whose wait outlasted the budget, the time PPU threads spent parked and the lever of the window. REWINDBOX_AUTO_STORM_CAPTURE_917: on a heavy PUTLLC storm the report asks once per boot for the heavy PUTLLC trace and a PPU region profile. Every lock is still taken in full and parks every PPU thread before the store; the relaxed PUTLLC is not used. No resolution, precision, frame limit, SPU count or priority, GETLLAR/PUTLLC delay or LLVM option changes. No codegen input changes: identities unchanged. Host bridge 8977315e unchanged; MoltenVK dependency of run 42733987255 (library d19d3a42). Built by the RPCS3 Core route (run 42772572060, attempt 1, source 1b910e42; Apple host harnesses run 42772572060 on 1b910e42). Verified offline on the downloaded artifacts with the repository verifier (pin_errors and bundle). Not measured on the iPhone; no FPS claim.",
